{"uid":"78f0c0741a8d779b","name":"test_a_superseded_detail_renders_response_is_discarded_not_applied","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub_refresh_loop#test_a_superseded_detail_renders_response_is_discarded_not_applied","historyId":"05c2d942010bdaa330e798d568329f05","time":{"start":1791942773700,"stop":1791942783570,"duration":9870},"description":"Targets the `myGen !== renderGeneration` / `seq !== loadSeq` guards\n    inside `renderRunDetail`'s `load()`. Several of the sub-renders that\n    `load()` drives (`renderTasks(document.getElementById(\"task-box\"), ...)`\n    among them) look their target element up fresh by `id` rather than via\n    a closure -- and every `renderRunDetail` call reuses the same ids. That\n    means a *stale* response landing after a later navigation has already\n    replaced the DOM does not write into a harmlessly-detached node; it\n    writes into the *live* page's element with the same id, because\n    `getElementById` finds whatever currently has that id. Only the\n    generation/sequence guards at the top of `load()` stop that stale write\n    from ever running. Reverting either guard (or removing `loadSeq`\n    entirely) makes the run-a marker task reappear in run-b's live task\n    list once the delayed response for run-a lands.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Targets the <code>myGen !== renderGeneration</code> / <code>seq !== loadSeq</code> guards<br />\ninside <code>renderRunDetail</code>'s <code>load()</code>. Several of the sub-renders that<br />\n<code>load()</code> drives (<code>renderTasks(document.getElementById(&quot;task-box&quot;), ...)</code><br />\namong them) look their target element up fresh by <code>id</code> rather than via<br />\na closure -- and every <code>renderRunDetail</code> call reuses the same ids. That<br />\nmeans a <em>stale</em> response landing after a later navigation has already<br />\nreplaced the DOM does not write into a harmlessly-detached node; it<br />\nwrites into the <em>live</em> page's element with the same id, because<br />\n<code>getElementById</code> finds whatever currently has that id. Only the<br />\ngeneration/sequence guards at the top of <code>load()</code> stop that stale write<br />\nfrom ever running. Reverting either guard (or removing <code>loadSeq</code><br />\nentirely) makes the run-a marker task reappear in run-b's live task<br />\nlist once the delayed response for run-a lands.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791941605405,"stop":1791941605405,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791941605406,"stop":1791941605406,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791942773698,"stop":1791942773698,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791942773698,"stop":1791942773699,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791942773699,"stop":1791942773699,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_wait_out_backoff_at_class_level","time":{"start":1791942773699,"stop":1791942773699